  "note": "Step 7 speculative fixture (derivation A): every expect is derived by hand from the 42-wire topology and the p.61-62 rule, not printed. ER-17 is diagram only and ER-18 a procedure note, so the wires are as printed. Topology: relays 1-4 latch through nH(+)-nG-nC-lamp-nE-coil-nF(-); pushbutton 6 (6Y on -) and pushbutton 1 (1Y on +) drive 1X/1V, which reaches 1E only through slide switch 1 LEFT; 1E feeds the arm 2V, and each switch 2-4 LEFT ties its relay's E to 1E while opening the path to higher-numbered switches, so only the lowest-numbered passenger is recognized. Lamp 5 hangs on 3L and lamp 6 on 4L; + reaches 1N/3K/4K when the farmer is home and the goose across, and 2N/3N/4N when the farmer is across and the goose home. Script choices, not printed: the objects carried (corn alone as a first error, goose with the wolf as an overload, farmer alone, corn home, farmer alone as the second error), and the order of slide-switch moves, chosen so that an E-junction tie only ever joins two relays in the same state (a tie across unlike states would put two coils behind one indicator lamp, an analogue case this fixture does not assert).",
